summary:
- topic: New Board Member
  text: The board extended a warm welcome to new board member Eleni Richardson.
- topic: FY2025 Budget
  text: The Superintendent reminded the community of the school budget referendum
    scheduled for Tuesday, June 10th, with all voting to take place at the community
    center. Information is available at tinyurl.com/schools26.
- topic: Personnel Resignations
  text: 'The resignations of three teachers were announced: Andrea Ernst (SEL teacher,
    Small/Kaler), Amy Hanlon (3rd grade, Kaler), and Sarah Barrett Robbins (4th grade,
    Kaler).'
- topic: Impact of Budget Cuts
  text: In response to a question, the Superintendent clarified that the announced
    resignations were not from individuals affected by a reduction in force. It was
    noted that the SEL teacher role was eliminated, but the individual resigned. A
    significant majority of staff whose positions were cut have been offered other
    roles within the district.
- topic: Personnel Elections
  text: The board unanimously approved the hiring of Megan Brand as an art teacher
    at SPHS and Alexandra Schlechty as a school counselor at Brown Elementary School.
- topic: New Job Description
  text: A new job description for a part-time Confidential Human Resources Assistant
    was unanimously approved. The position is part of a district office reorganization
    that resulted in a net reduction of salary costs.
- topic: Executive Session
  text: The board voted to enter an executive session to discuss a confidential personnel
    matter.
